---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ComingSoon from '../../components/ComingSoon.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Drones — Use Case"
  description="Survey and inspection event detection over long flights — timestamped events instead of hours of footage review."
  canonicalPath="/use-cases/drones"
  mdTwin="/use-cases/drones.md"
>
  <div class="page">
    <a class="back" href="/use-cases">← Use cases</a>
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Drones / UAV</p>
      <h1>Understood, not just recorded</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Timestamped events instead of hours of footage review.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content">
      <p>
        A two-hour inspection flight produces two hours of footage. Without scene understanding,
        that footage requires a human reviewer to watch every second. With Primate Vision,
        you ask a question — "flag any section of fence with visible damage" or "identify
        moments when a person enters the restricted zone" — and get back a list of timestamped
        events with annotated evidence clips. The flight becomes a structured log, not a
        video file.
      </p>
      <p>
        Darwin's edge-capable architecture runs on Jetson-grade hardware for onboard inference,
        eliminating the cloud round-trip that makes real-time aerial analysis impractical.
        For post-flight batch processing, the same model processes footage at significantly
        faster-than-realtime speeds. Either way, the output is deterministic: the same flight
        footage produces the same event list, every time.
      </p>

      <ComingSoon note="Drone survey workflow guide and edge deployment examples — coming soon." />
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 128px 24px 192px; }
  .back { font-size: var(--fs-body-sm); color: var(--color-text-muted); display: block; margin-bottom: 64px; }
  .back:hover { color: var(--color-signal); }
  .hero { margin-bottom: 80px; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-footnote);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--color-signal);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  h1 { font-size: var(--fs-h1); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .lede { font-size: var(--fs-body-lg); color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
  .content p { font-size: var(--fs-body-lg); line-height: 1.75; color: var(--color-text-primary); opacity: 0.85; margin: 0 0 32px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { h1 { font-size: var(--fs-h2); } .page { padding: 88px 20px 128px; } }
</style>
